Give a differently-classified fresh capability its own root

`VarInTypeTree.normalizeLocalCaps` hides every fresh capability that reached
an inferred value type in the type's declaration root, asserting that each can
be classified like that root. Two fresh capabilities of unrelated classifiers
— a shared strategy from a polymorphic given beside an unscoped sink from an
inline given, bound into one inlined proxy — therefore crashed the compiler
with "attempting to add any to {any} of value x$proxy1" instead of producing a
diagnostic or a type.

A classifier mismatch means the capability cannot be hidden here, which the
method already expresses for level failures by returning false; the caller
then mints a further declaration root for it. The inferred type carries one
root per classifier, which `inDeclRoots` already allows.

